1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Product teams have great growth ideas, but turning them into measurable experiments and safely releasing winning changes takes time. PulsePilot AI changes that.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:44,000
With PulsePilot, a product manager simply describes a growth objective. Google Gemini transforms that objective into an experiment strategy, while specialized AI agents coordinate experiment design, analytics, release safety and growth recommendations.

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:09,000
PulsePilot connects directly to Flagsmith Cloud. It provisions multivariate feature flags, evaluates user identities and verifies remote configuration changes. This is real feature-flag infrastructure, not a simulated integration.

4
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Different users receive different checkout experiences through Flagsmith identity evaluation. The same application can deliver a multi-step control experience or a single-page treatment without hardcoded client-side experiment assignment.

5
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:59,000
PulsePilot calculates experiment statistics deterministically, not through an AI guess. Our current checkout dataset shows a 20.2 percent relative uplift, but a p-value of 0.134 and a confidence interval crossing zero. The platform correctly identifies the experiment as underpowered instead of declaring a premature winner.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Production changes require human oversight. The Release Guardian evaluates the available evidence, presents the configuration diff and requires explicit authorization before a permitted Flagsmith rollout. Every operation is verified against the remote configuration.

7
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Every important operation is recorded in a tamper-evident SHA-256 audit chain. PulsePilot AI connects intelligent experimentation with real feature management and responsible production releases.

